# 20260912T192557-1001-192-168-30-105-22097.wav
#
# The first call modec placed to the reference modem rather than taking
# one from it: modec dials the ATA, the CX93001 answers pinned to V.32 at
# 4800 (AT+MS=V32,0,4800,4800).  The only live fixture where a real
# answering V.32 modem is not 2600.network, and the only one that starts
# before the far end has answered.
#
# It pins three faults of the calling start-up, each of which alone kept
# this call from ever connecting.  The first seconds are baresip's
# 440 + 480 Hz ringback, which the caller used to take for AC -- AA at
# 0.32 s and a 40 ms round trip.  The answerer's R1 goes on arriving for
# a second after our S begins, and the caller used to read it as R3.  And
# R3 and E read through this line's inter-symbol interference from the raw
# symbols came back 17% wrong, so the one E went by unrecognised.  Before
# the fixes the replay reads 0 bytes; after, CONNECT at 19.78 s and all
# eight of the reference's payload lines.  See reference-modem.md, "Roles
# reversed: modec dials".
source:    recordings/20260912T192557-1001-192-168-30-105-22097.wav
seconds:   40.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32
v8:        no
connect:   V32 4800
retrains:  0
expect:    B0007 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
tolerance: 0
